From e0d26351bb6029b06c9036761ec364c3c69e351e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:54:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] shader: CompileProgram clears the SRT reads' values with the
 storage they lived in

CompileProgram frees value_storage, which holds the instructions the SRT
reads' values point to, then MarkTrackedWrites' runtime validator follows a
ReadConst into srt_reads[slot].value: a use-after-free. In Marvel's
Wolverine (title scene, Linux) the freed node read as an argument-less
Identity and the precompile or compute-ahead worker stopped with
"index >= self.NumArgs()" (Value.h). The values are cleared with their
storage; the validator then treats those reads as not host-evaluable, the
conservative answer. Nothing after the clear reads them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/shader/recompiler/ShaderRecompiler.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/graphics/shader/recompiler/ShaderRecompiler.cpp b/src/graphics/shader/recompiler/ShaderRecompiler.cpp
index dc858729..096c3e27 100644
--- a/src/graphics/shader/recompiler/ShaderRecompiler.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/shader/recompiler/ShaderRecompiler.cpp
@@ -779,6 +779,11 @@ CompileResult CompileProgram(TranslateResult translated, const CompileOptions& o
 	}
 	IR::DropBoundDescriptorWords(ir);
 	ir.value_storage.clear();
+	// The SRT reads' values lived in value_storage: emptied, MarkTrackedWrites' validator would follow freed
+	// instructions (a fatal "index >= NumArgs" in the precompile, Marvel's Wolverine's title on Linux).
+	for (auto& read: ir.srt_reads) {
+		read.value = {};
+	}
 	IR::RemoveIdentities(ir);
 	IR::EliminateDeadCode(ir.blocks);
 	IR::BranchResult branches;
-- 
